Notebook[
 {
  Cell[
   "Generic unequal-charge BMPV four-derivative correction exact in rotation"\
, "Title"], Cell["Version-3 human notation guide (documentation only; no \
Input cell is changed). In the compact solution and verifier notebooks: \
x=r^2; q1,q2,q3 are the harmonic parameters mu1,mu2,mu3, not normalized \
conserved charges; jrot is the rotation parameter j; U1,U2,U3 are the \
electric corrections delta u_I; B1,B2,B3 are the gauge-covariant fibre \
corrections; Om is delta omega; Ft, Gr, and Sq are the temporal warp, radial \
warp, and squashing corrections; P and S are delta p and delta s, where \
X1=exp(2p/3-s), X2=exp(2p/3+s), and X3=exp(-4p/3). Physical quantities are \
Q_I=Pi mu_I/(4 G5) and J1=J2=Pi j/(4 G5). See the report section \
'Human-readable notation and result at a glance' for the full dictionary.", 
   "Text"], 
  Cell["Self-contained closed solution and exact validation ledger", 
   "Subtitle"], Cell["Scope", "Section"], Cell["The correction is first order \
in lambda3 and exact in the rotation parameter jrot. The even sector \
terminates at jrot^2 and the odd sector terminates at jrot^3. No external \
file is required to inspect the expressions embedded below.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Conventions", "Section"], Cell[BoxData["ClearAll[x,q1,q2,q3,jrot,H1,H\
2,H3,Delta]; H1=x+q1; H2=x+q2; H3=x+q3; Delta=H1 H2+H1 H3+H2 H3;"], "Input"], 
  Cell["Complete correction fields", "Section"], 
  Cell["These are the lambda3 correction fields in areal gauge at fixed Page \
charges, with asymptotic decay and no added 1/x rotation-parameter mode. A \
complete generic higher-derivative Wald angular-momentum calculation is not \
claimed by this notebook.", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"exactSolution", "=", 
      RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", RowBox[
         {RowBox[{"\"Gauge\"", "\[Rule]", "\"dhr=0; areal x=r^2; fixed Page \
charges; no added 1/x rotation mode\""}], ",", RowBox[{"\"OrderInLambda3\"", 
            "\[Rule]", "1"}], ",", RowBox[{"\"RotationDependence\"", 
            "\[Rule]", "\"exact finite polynomial through jrot^3\""}], ",", 
